// Windows child #5 (companion to ../mainwindows.bit, #5801): MANY SMALL
// print() calls to stdout through the real capture pipe -- childtrunc_windows
// .bit's own comment flagged this exact path ("a many-small-writes-to-a-
// redirected-pipe path on Windows stdout independently needs its own
// investigation") as out of #5782's scope; #5801 is that investigation.
// 40,000 calls of a 98-byte line (97 'a's + '\n') = 3,920,000 bytes, kept
// under `osRunCaptureMaxBytes` (4 MiB / 4,194,304) so the capture cannot
// truncate and the comparison in testManyPrints below is exact rather than
// capped. Exit 0.
fn main() {
  let line = "aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\n" // 98 bytes
  let i = 0
  while (i < 40000) {
    print(line)
    i = i + 1
  }
}
